WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:02.280
Instructor: This is going to be a very quick video.

00:02.280 --> 00:03.780
I just need to explain one thing

00:03.780 --> 00:04.978
that we haven't run into yet.

00:04.978 --> 00:07.830
If I'm on a branch and I have some work

00:07.830 --> 00:09.870
that is not currently committed,

00:09.870 --> 00:11.820
so let's go to the oldies branch,

00:11.820 --> 00:15.460
git switch oldies, and I'll do some work here.

00:15.460 --> 00:18.837
I'll add two Van Morrison songs, great songs,

00:18.837 --> 00:20.700
and it's "Stoned Me" and "Caravan."

00:20.700 --> 00:24.570
So I'll save those two, but I'm not gonna add any commits.

00:24.570 --> 00:26.760
So over here I see git status,

00:26.760 --> 00:29.550
I modified that, I have changes that are not staged.

00:29.550 --> 00:32.880
There's work on this branch that has not been committed.

00:32.880 --> 00:34.844
If I try and switch branches right now,

00:34.844 --> 00:36.450
let's see what happens.

00:36.450 --> 00:38.310
Let's go back to the,

00:38.310 --> 00:43.083
how about our empty playlist, git switch empty playlist,

00:44.310 --> 00:45.930
and what does it say?

00:45.930 --> 00:46.920
I get an error.

00:46.920 --> 00:48.840
Your local changes to the following files

00:48.840 --> 00:50.850
would be overwritten by checkout.

00:50.850 --> 00:52.500
Playlist dot txt.

00:52.500 --> 00:55.170
It's telling me that the work I have done right now

00:55.170 --> 00:57.780
that I have not yet committed, which is right here,

00:57.780 --> 00:59.910
if I try and switch to a different branch

00:59.910 --> 01:02.369
it's gonna be lost because it's not committed.

01:02.369 --> 01:04.200
This branch doesn't know about it.

01:04.200 --> 01:06.210
There's not gonna be a bookmark for it

01:06.210 --> 01:09.690
in the really large book before we change pages.

01:09.690 --> 01:13.363
So it says, "Please commit your changes or stash them."

01:13.363 --> 01:15.296
We will learn more about stashing

01:15.296 --> 01:17.610
in just a couple of sections from now.

01:17.610 --> 01:19.080
So for now, that's not an option.

01:19.080 --> 01:21.420
For now, our only option is to commit our work

01:21.420 --> 01:24.630
or just delete it I guess, and not make those changes.

01:24.630 --> 01:29.280
So I am gonna commit that, git add playlist,

01:29.280 --> 01:33.513
git commit, dash m, add two Van Morrison songs.

01:35.716 --> 01:37.194
Just like that.

01:37.194 --> 01:39.240
And now I can switch.

01:39.240 --> 01:42.330
So I can do the same command to switch to empty playlist.

01:42.330 --> 01:43.470
No complaints.

01:43.470 --> 01:45.360
So if you run into an issue like this,

01:45.360 --> 01:47.760
hopefully you understand why now Git is warning you

01:47.760 --> 01:49.500
you're going to lose those changes.

01:49.500 --> 01:50.760
You either need to stash them,

01:50.760 --> 01:53.010
which we haven't learned, or commit them.

01:53.010 --> 01:54.585
Now the last example I showed you,

01:54.585 --> 01:57.930
we had changes that were in conflict,

01:57.930 --> 01:59.700
right when I tried to switch branches,

01:59.700 --> 02:03.330
we were working on the same file, this playlist file

02:03.330 --> 02:05.520
and they were in conflict.

02:05.520 --> 02:06.727
And so Git yelled at me and said,

02:06.727 --> 02:08.100
"Hey, I don't know what to do."

02:08.100 --> 02:10.620
We'll learn more about conflicts when we get to merging

02:10.620 --> 02:13.230
but sometimes that's not an issue at all.

02:13.230 --> 02:15.415
So if I make a new file, for example,

02:15.415 --> 02:19.470
I'm on the oldies branch, lemme make a new branch here,

02:19.470 --> 02:22.110
git switch dash C,

02:22.110 --> 02:26.050
and this branch will be, I don't know, how about chicken?

02:27.761 --> 02:29.430
I'm gonna delete it.

02:29.430 --> 02:31.170
A chicken branch, okay?

02:31.170 --> 02:32.460
And on this chicken branch,

02:32.460 --> 02:36.600
I'm gonna make a new file entirely called chickens dot txt.

02:36.600 --> 02:38.220
And I'll put some of my chickens in here,

02:38.220 --> 02:40.320
like Stevie Chicks.

02:40.320 --> 02:42.856
Okay, so I have this new file no other branch has

02:42.856 --> 02:45.954
but I haven't added or committed that file.

02:45.954 --> 02:49.740
And so now if I switch again, let's go back to oldies.

02:49.740 --> 02:51.199
Git switch oldies.

02:51.199 --> 02:53.518
Previously at the beginning of this video

02:53.518 --> 02:57.570
we saw that Git yelled at me when I tried to switch

02:57.570 --> 02:58.403
and it says,

02:58.403 --> 02:59.688
"You can't switch.

02:59.688 --> 03:00.810
You have changes that are gonna be overwritten

03:00.810 --> 03:02.100
that are in conflict.

03:02.100 --> 03:03.150
We don't know what to do.

03:03.150 --> 03:04.770
Please stash or commit them."

03:04.770 --> 03:06.120
But this is going to be different

03:06.120 --> 03:08.430
because no other branch has this file.

03:08.430 --> 03:11.387
There's no way that it's in conflict with anything.

03:11.387 --> 03:14.250
So what actually will happen is this file

03:14.250 --> 03:16.020
is gonna come with me.

03:16.020 --> 03:19.980
I'm now on the oldies branch and I still have chickens.

03:19.980 --> 03:20.813
Do you see that?

03:20.813 --> 03:22.080
The file's still there.

03:22.080 --> 03:23.947
And it came with me and it still says,

03:23.947 --> 03:25.356
"Hey, there's this untracked file.

03:25.356 --> 03:27.240
You haven't made a commit with it anywhere.

03:27.240 --> 03:29.484
It's just gonna follow you to every branch you go to."

03:29.484 --> 03:33.990
So for now, I'm just gonna recommend we always add

03:33.990 --> 03:36.720
and commit changes before we switch branches

03:36.720 --> 03:38.040
so that we can avoid this.

03:38.040 --> 03:39.150
But of course, like I said,

03:39.150 --> 03:41.880
we're gonna learn how to stash changes very soon.

03:41.880 --> 03:43.560
First, we're gonna learn about merging

03:43.560 --> 03:45.840
but I just wanted to call your attention to this behavior.

03:45.840 --> 03:48.120
When you switch branches, sometimes,

03:48.120 --> 03:51.900
if you have unstaged changes, they will come with you.

03:51.900 --> 03:54.630
Other times if they're in conflict, Git will yell at you,

03:54.630 --> 03:55.803
so just know that.
